Contracts for this area: `docs/DB_FIELD_CONTRACT_GRANTS.md`, `docs/DB_FIELD_CONTRACT_DONOR_REPORTS_V2_DELTA.md`, `docs/DB_FIELD_CONTRACT_UPLOADED_DOCUMENTS_V2_DELTA.md`, `docs/REPORT_REQUIREMENT_SNAPSHOT_SCHEMA.md`, `docs/API_CONTRACT_ME_V2.md`. Read the one your task touches before editing.

- Report structure comes from `requirement_snapshot_json`. Do not read `funder_report_templates` for structure; do not add authored slugs, archetypes, hint maps or funder-owned lists anywhere.
- Facts: V2 shape and key grammar (`<domain>.<entity>.<facet>[.<period>][.<scope>]`). Milestone ≠ target ≠ actual ≠ baseline. A conflict needs equal metric, period and scope. Supersede; never delete.
- Money without currency is unconfirmed. Percentages, variances and totals are `derived` facts written by code; the model cites them.
- The evidence matrix is the single satisfaction judgement. Do not add a second "is this satisfied" path anywhere.
- Gate replies compile to actions with echoes; no free text becomes a fact.
- Every returned enum has a `_label` sibling. No agent, model or stage name in any user-facing label.
- Generic fallback is never merged into a funder-specific snapshot.
- Extraction isolation, resume/idempotency and the kill switch are not to be weakened by any change.
